  "findings": [
    "On the actual shipped path, un-merging all reachable kinds in all 50 blocks leaves mlp.fc2 merged: 0.013150 becomes 0.010263, or 1.0963x the base error. It recovers 76.2% of the stochastic merge gap, not the whole gap.",
    "The original deterministic RTN, hypothetical four-kind curve runs 0.010452 to 0.009362 (1.1164x). It remains for provenance and is not the shipped unmerged_blocks result.",
    "THERE IS NO HOT SUBSET on the deployable arm. Reachable stochastic gain spans 1.836x across 50 blocks; worst-5 recovers 12.6% of the reachable gap against 10% for an arbitrary 5, and the largest sampled targeting premium is 9.9 points. Selecting all 50 recovers the reachable gap at +2.4% arithmetic FLOPs but still leaves fc2 merged.",
    "The 7-block list and the old order [49, 15, 20, 11, 7, 10, 18, 23, 14, 17] describe the deterministic four-kind hypothetical. The shipped three-kind stochastic order starts [7, 20, 15, 11, 8, 10, 9, 6, 14, 23]. This is a stored-weight compute-allocation order, not a network-sensitivity or perceptual-quality ranking.",
    "INFLATION AND STORED ERROR RANK KINDS OPPOSITELY. attn.qkv_proj has the highest inflation (1.1636) and the lowest error before PDD (0.00883); attn.out_proj has the highest error before PDD (0.01041) and nearly the lowest inflation (1.0990). 'Which kind quantises worst' and 'which kind PDD damages most' are different questions and the answers are reversed."
